<title>UK: SFO says to probe Eurotunnel share deals. [CORRECTED 22:38 GMT]</title>
<headline>SFO says to probe Eurotunnel share deals. [CORRECTED 22:38 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline from &quot;Fraud probe ordered into Eurotunnel shares-police&quot;, to omit reference to police.)</p>
<p>Britain's Serious Fraud Office (SFO) said on Sunday it would investigate allegations of market manipulation in shares of Eurotunnel Plc on behalf of French police.</p>
<p>&quot;The SFO has agreed to investigate on behalf of the French authorities allegations of market manipulation in Eurotunnel shares,&quot; SFO spokesman James O'Donoghue told Reuters.  </p>
<p>The information gathered by the SFO will be for the French authorities,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't have grounds to investigate allegations of market manipulation on a domestic level,&quot; the spokesman said.</p>
<p>-- Astrid Zweynert London newsroom +44 171 542 7792</p>
</text>
